    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 78.23 projection, bolstered by a prime matchup against Michael Wacha and a wind-out scenario that elevates his power-speed upside. He is joined by **Vinnie Pasquantino** (73.84) and **Isaac Paredes** (70.11) as our primary anchors; **Vinnie Pasquantino** thrives today against Corbin Burnes due to a massive +14% dynamic platoon edge, while **Isaac Paredes** benefits from favorable park factors and high-leverage lineup placement. **James Wood** also provides a high-floor start (65.25) leading off against Casey Mize, as his elite xwOBA metrics allow him to bypass the modest park penalty and secure a lock for the leadoff spot.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our bench, where **Josh Naylor** (55.21) narrowly missed the final lineup. While **Josh Naylor** provides reliable production, the optimizer prioritized the positional versatility and dynamic platoon advantages offered by **Max Muncy** and **Austin Riley**, despite their lower raw scores. We are also keeping a close eye on **Mickey Moniak**, whose score of 54.76 is heavily suppressed by an unfavorable matchup against the talented Cam Schlittler; his +14% platoon edge is the only reason he remains in the starting nine over the surging **Trevor Story**, who remains a high-variance bench option against a left-handed arm.\n\nRisks remain present across the board as every projected spot relies on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. **Brice Turang** faces a significant hurdle against David Peterson, where his efficiency score (57.91) is dampened by Peterson\u2019s elite ability to hold runners, effectively neutralizing the stolen base upside that typically makes **Brice Turang** a must-start. Managers should also be cautious with **Mickey Moniak** and **Jose Caballero**, as both players are facing SPs with high skill ratings that threaten to drag their performance below the 50-point threshold. Monitor the official lineups closely, as any shift down the batting order for **Austin Riley** or **Zach McKinstry** could force an immediate mid-afternoon substitution.",
